  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday through Saturday)\nIssued at 1247 PM MDT Sun Oct 4 2026\n\nAn upper level low currently moving onshore northern CA will drift \neast into the Great Basin Tuesday, meander east/southeast across NM \nWednesday and Thursday, then into south TX by Friday. Improving lift \nwith the upper level wave, a 60kt speed max, and sufficient moisture \nand instability will allow a couple showers to develop over the high \nterrain each afternoon. Rainfall chances remain very low and precip \namounts are light so this activity is mainly to have little impact \noutside some localized gusty winds. Temps will stay within +/-5F of \nnormal thru Thursday with the warmest values focused over eastern NM.\n\nA poorly defined upper level shortwave ridge will attempt to form\nover northern NM Friday and Saturday before breaking down ahead \nof a broader upper level trough approaching from the PacNW. Temps\nwill near normal in this pattern. Light winds Friday will give \nway to slight southwest breezes by Saturday over eastern NM. The \nweather pattern will likely become more active beginning Sunday \nbut there is still a lot of uncertainty with the broader synoptic\npattern across the western U.S.",
